# =============================================================================
#  Things that must never be committed
# =============================================================================
# Whoever holds this can mint licence keys for every copy ever sold, and there is
# no way to revoke keys already issued. Losing it is bad; publishing it is fatal.
cmake/licence-secret.txt

# Minted keys are stock -- 5,000 of them. Committing these is giving the product away.
keys*.csv

# Signs activation tokens. The public half beside it is committed on purpose; this half
# would let anyone mint an activation for any machine.
cmake/activation-private-key.SECRET.txt
*.SECRET.txt

# Supabase URL, publishable key, PayPal client id. The publishable ones are safe in a
# browser but not worth putting in a repo, and this is the file a real secret would end
# up in by accident.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
lost-website/.env
lost-website/.env.*
!lost-website/.env.example

# =============================================================================
#  Build output and dependencies -- all refetchable
# =============================================================================
# CMake build tree, JUCE checkout, WebView2 SDK. ~1.9 GB.
.dist/

# Built VST3 bundle and the installer. ~95 MB, rebuilt by CMake.
plugin/

# The installer again, where the site serves it from.
#
# It was tracked here until the first push, and it is the reason .git had reached 124 MB:
# git keeps every version forever, so each rebuild left another 36 MB in history that
# nothing could ever reclaim. Four copies were already in there.
#
# The build writes it back into this folder every time, and for a deployed site it belongs
# in Supabase Storage rather than in the repo -- the releases row already carries the size
# and the SHA-256 that identify which build is current.
lost-website/public/downloads/

# JUCE copies its frontend bridge in here at configure time.
ui/src/juce/

ui/node_modules/
ui/dist/
lost-website/node_modules/
lost-website/dist/

# Third-party plug-in kept for reference only. Not ours to redistribute, and 30 MB.
backend plugin/

# =============================================================================
#  The website lives in its own repository
# =============================================================================
# github.com/NoobKodak/LOSTDUCK-Website -- which is also what Vercel builds.
#
# It used to be committed here as well. Keeping both meant a subtree split and two pushes
# after every change, and the first time one was forgotten the two copies would disagree
# with nothing to say which was right. The folder stays on disk because that is where it
# is worked on; it is simply tracked by the other repository, not this one.
#
# Clone it alongside if this working copy is ever set up fresh.
lost-website/

# =============================================================================
#  Editor and OS noise
# =============================================================================
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store

# Local scratch
*.log
*.local

# Archives whose contents are already extracted next to them.
*.zip
